Subject: dyn_load: load NVML in place of the CUDA driver and cuRAND, without libloading
Why: hex-gpu reads NVIDIA GPUs through NVML (docs/design/gpu-telemetry.md G1), which cuda-rust does not bind; its CUDA driver loader's policy is what carries over: try each library name in turn, WSL's own path among them, keep the library loaded for the process, and report a library that did not load apart from one missing a symbol. The library is opened through Hex's own FFI file (crates/hex-gpu/src/nvml/sys.rs, CLAUDE.md §12) rather than libloading, which Hex does not link; the expect on the candidate list goes (CLAUDE.md §1); NVML is initialised once and never shut down, so device handles stay valid; and a failed load is not cached, so a driver loaded after the node started is found at its next open.

